Hillary, maybe I could be your best friend.
希拉里，也许我可以演你的好闺蜜。

486
00:21:10.800 --> 00:21:11.960
This is it.
就是这样。

487
00:21:11.960 --> 00:21:13.980
And then I could go just for a week, John.
然后我就可以只去一周，约翰。

488
00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:15.400
Just like four days.
就四天左右。

489
00:21:15.780 --> 00:21:15.980
Yeah.
是啊。

490
00:21:16.260 --> 00:21:16.400
Okay.
好的。

491
00:21:16.800 --> 00:21:17.280
There.
搞定。

492
00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:17.940
We worked it out.
我们谈妥了。

493
00:21:18.020 --> 00:21:18.540
Jen Salata.
简·萨拉塔。

494
00:21:18.800 --> 00:21:20.200
Jen Salata directs it.
简·萨拉塔执导。

495
00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:20.800
Make it happen.
让它成真吧。

496
00:21:21.020 --> 00:21:24.240
Well, Hillary Sank was 20 years old when she was in Next Karate Kid.
希拉里·斯万克出演《新小子难缠》时才20岁。

497
00:21:24.460 --> 00:21:29.640
When she was 25 years old, she did the lead role in Boys Don't Cry.
25岁时，她主演了《男孩别哭》。

498
00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:30.560
Wow.
哇。

499
00:21:30.880 --> 00:21:32.460
And she won an Oscar.
并且她赢得了奥斯卡奖。

500
00:21:32.820 --> 00:21:35.960
She is one of the youngest women to ever win an Oscar.
她是史上最年轻的奥斯卡影后之一。

501
00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:40.540
She also won an Oscar for her lead role in Million Dollar Baby.
她还凭借在《百万美元宝贝》中的主角戏份赢得了奥斯卡奖。

502
00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:42.160
That movie destroyed me.
那部电影简直让我心碎。

503
00:21:42.380 --> 00:21:42.720
Ugh.
唉。

504
00:21:42.840 --> 00:21:43.740
I mean, both of those movies.
我是说，这两部电影都是。

505
00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:45.160
I mean, they're, ugh.
我是说，它们，唉。

506
00:21:45.440 --> 00:21:51.580
There are only 12 other actresses who have won two or more lead actress Oscars.
只有另外12位女演员曾获得过两座或以上的奥斯卡最佳女主角奖。

507
00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:53.660
Those are both lead actress Oscars.
这两座都是最佳女主角奖。

508
00:21:53.860 --> 00:21:55.940
So she's in a very impressive club there.
所以她加入了一个非常了不起的俱乐部。

509
00:21:56.080 --> 00:21:56.940
She sure is.
确实如此。

510
00:21:57.220 --> 00:21:59.120
So that's Hillary Swank, y'all.
所以，这就是希拉里·斯万克，各位。

511
00:21:59.360 --> 00:22:01.080
Well, Hillary, we are here for you.
好吧，希拉里，我们支持你。

512
00:22:01.280 --> 00:22:02.560
We should take a break.
我们该休息一下了。

513
00:22:02.700 --> 00:22:03.720
And we come back.
等我们回来。

514
00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:06.060
There is a classic Jim Prank.
会有一个经典的吉姆恶作剧。

515
00:22:12.580 --> 00:22:15.940
Attention all new and existing members of the WDNC.
请注意，所有WDNC的新老成员。

516
00:22:16.200 --> 00:22:19.760
I'm Melanie Sanders, and this is the We Do Not Care Club podcaSt.
我是梅兰妮·桑德斯，这是“我们不在乎俱乐部”播客。

517
00:22:20.220 --> 00:22:24.020
We got to midlife and realized we just simply do not care much anymore.
我们到了中年才意识到，我们真的没那么在乎了。

518
00:22:24.280 --> 00:22:32.120
Now, we got to help each other make sense of hot flashes, itchy ears, chin hair, trifling families, brain fog, and bat wings.
现在，我们要互相帮助，去理解潮热、耳朵发痒、下巴长毛、琐碎的家庭事务、脑雾和蝴蝶袖。

519
00:22:32.340 --> 00:22:35.000
We are not alone, and we will be heard.
我们并不孤单，我们的声音会被听见。

520
00:22:35.100 --> 00:22:36.880
So come join the WDNC.
所以快来加入WDNC吧。

521
00:22:36.880 --> 00:22:42.280
Follow and listen to the We Do Not Care Club podcast with Melanie Sanders wherever you get your podcaSt.
在任何收听播客的地方，关注并收听梅兰妮·桑德斯的“我们不在乎俱乐部”播客。

522
00:22:45.360 --> 00:22:49.280
This episode opens with everyone just working at their desks.
这一集开场时，大家都在办公桌前工作。

523
00:22:49.440 --> 00:22:50.420
We're just working.
我们只是在工作。

524
00:22:50.520 --> 00:22:51.280
Just a normal day.
就是普通的一天。

525
00:22:51.440 --> 00:22:51.900
No biggie.
没什么大不了的。

526
00:22:52.140 --> 00:22:56.980
But then Dwight discovers a red wire that's plugged into his computer.
但随后德怀特发现有一根红线插在他的电脑上。

527
00:22:57.120 --> 00:22:58.380
No other computers have red wires.
其他电脑都没有红线。

528
00:22:58.580 --> 00:22:59.040
What is it?
那是什么？

529
00:22:59.240 --> 00:23:00.340
Yeah, it's a new wire.
对，那是一根新线。

530
00:23:00.360 --> 00:23:01.660
It's never been there before.
以前从来没见过。

531
00:23:01.920 --> 00:23:02.180
Yeah.
是啊。

532
00:23:02.340 --> 00:23:04.520
Well, he starts tearing at this wire.
嗯，他开始扯这根线。

533
00:23:04.780 --> 00:23:06.360
Yeah, he wants to know where it's coming from.
对，他想知道这线是从哪儿来的。

534
00:23:06.500 --> 00:23:06.680
Yeah.
是啊。

535
00:23:06.680 --> 00:23:11.100
In the script, it says, Dwight pulls the wire off the floor and follows it to the wall.
剧本里写的是，德怀特把线从地板上拉起来，顺着线一直跟到墙边。

536
00:23:11.280 --> 00:23:17.240
It goes over a door frame under Phyllis's desk, and Dwight crawls under Phyllis's desk.
它穿过门框，到了菲利斯的桌子底下，德怀特就爬到了菲利斯的桌子底下。

537
00:23:17.620 --> 00:23:19.380
Oh, we did it a little differently.
哦，我们拍的时候稍微改动了一下。

538
00:23:19.540 --> 00:23:20.580
We did it a little differently.
我们拍的时候稍微改动了一下。

539
00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:25.700
First of all, you can't crawl through Phyllis's desk because there was like a backstop, right?
首先，你没法爬过菲利斯的桌子，因为后面有个挡板，对吧？

540
00:23:25.860 --> 00:23:25.980
Yeah.
对。

541
00:23:26.140 --> 00:23:28.440
So it doesn't go all the way through to Stanley's desk.
所以它没法一直通到斯坦利的桌子那边。

542
00:23:28.800 --> 00:23:31.640
And in the script, Phyllis says, Dwight, get out of there.
剧本里菲利斯说的是：“德怀特，从那儿出来。”

543
00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:33.600
And that's pretty much in the episode.
这一段在正片里基本保留了。

544
00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:35.920
And then Dwight would have said, shush, shush, shush.
然后德怀特本该说：“嘘，嘘，嘘。”

545
00:23:36.440 --> 00:23:38.560
But I think Rain improvise.
但我认为雷恩即兴发挥了。

546
00:23:38.740 --> 00:23:39.680
Shut up, Phyllis.
“闭嘴，菲利斯。”

547
00:23:41.620 --> 00:23:44.200
So Dwight's going to follow this wire into the hall.
所以德怀特要顺着这根线一直跟到走廊里。

548
00:23:44.480 --> 00:23:54.300
Yeah, all the way outside and up a telephone pole, which we can see over Jim's shoulder in Jim's talking head.
对，一直跟到外面，爬上一根电线杆，我们在吉姆的单人访谈镜头里，能从他肩膀后面看到那根杆子。

549
00:23:54.440 --> 00:23:54.760
Right.
没错。

550
00:23:54.900 --> 00:23:56.520
And it is a real telephone pole.
而且那是一根真正的电线杆。

551
00:23:56.740 --> 00:23:57.960
It's a real telephone pole.
那真的是一根电线杆。

552
00:23:57.960 --> 00:24:02.860
Well, Jim says he got 500 feet of red wire at a flea market for 20 bucks.
吉姆说他在跳蚤市场花了20美元买了500英尺的红线。

553
00:24:03.420 --> 00:24:05.000
How long did this take him?
他花了多久弄这个？

554
00:24:05.100 --> 00:24:06.680
Jim has a lot of extra time.
吉姆有很多闲暇时间。

555
00:24:06.860 --> 00:24:08.940
He gets to work so early.
他上班去得太早了。

556
00:24:09.180 --> 00:24:10.800
I feel like Pam is like, you know what?
我觉得帕姆当时的想法是，你知道吗？

557
00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:16.980
I know we were going to carpool, but you've got that Dwight prank, and you've got to go at three in the morning, and I'm going to sleep in.
我知道我们本来要拼车，但你要搞那个捉弄德怀特的恶作剧，还得凌晨三点出发，所以我还是睡懒觉吧。

558
00:24:17.280 --> 00:24:17.720
Yeah.
没错。

559
00:24:17.720 --> 00:24:21.660
Like, what's the real life side of that?
那现实生活中会是什么样呢？

560
00:24:22.580 --> 00:24:27.900
I reached out to Randy to find out how we did this stunt of Rain up on this telephone pole.
我联系了兰迪，想了解我们是怎么拍雷恩在电线杆上那个特技镜头的。

561
00:24:28.100 --> 00:24:28.320
Right.
对。

562
00:24:28.400 --> 00:24:29.940
He can't climb a real telephone pole.
他不可能爬上真正的电线杆。

563
00:24:30.020 --> 00:24:30.900
That's not safe.
那不安全。

564
00:24:31.080 --> 00:24:42.320
No, because what he told me was that the pole over Jim's shoulder really is an actual working utility pole that's embedded in our sidewalk, you know, right out there.
不，因为他告诉我，吉姆肩膀后面的那根电线杆确实是一根正在使用的公用电线杆，就埋在我们外面的人行道上。

565
00:24:42.560 --> 00:24:44.600
Folks, don't go climb it for a photo.
各位，千万别为了拍照去爬它。

566
00:24:44.840 --> 00:24:45.240
Don't climb it.
别爬。

567
00:24:45.240 --> 00:24:46.400
You can get electrocuted.
你会触电的。

568
00:24:46.400 --> 00:24:48.720
Yeah, it carried high-voltage electricity.
是的，上面有高压电。

569
00:24:48.800 --> 00:24:52.820
They couldn't even have a stunt person dressed as Dwight climb that pole.
他们甚至不能让替身演员打扮成德怀特去爬那根杆子。

570
00:24:52.980 --> 00:24:53.220
Yeah.
是啊。

571
00:24:53.440 --> 00:25:00.440
So, our production designer, Michael Gallenberg, and his construction team rented a matching utility pole.
所以，我们的美术指导迈克尔·加伦伯格和他的施工团队租了一根一模一样的电线杆。

572
00:25:00.780 --> 00:25:02.720
You can do that, I guess.
我想这居然也能租到。

573
00:25:02.840 --> 00:25:03.000
No.
不。

574
00:25:03.500 --> 00:25:04.560
Where is that?
那东西在哪儿？

575
00:25:04.820 --> 00:25:08.180
I mean, seriously, how do they know these things?
我是说，说真的，他们是怎么知道这些门道的？

576
00:25:08.540 --> 00:25:10.860
This is the crazy part of Hollywood magic.
这就是好莱坞魔法疯狂的地方。

577
00:25:11.080 --> 00:25:12.300
Oh, you know what I'm going to do today?
哦，你知道我今天要做什么吗？

578
00:25:12.400 --> 00:25:14.760
I'm going to rent a fakie telephone pole.
我要去租一根假电线杆。

579
00:25:14.920 --> 00:25:15.140
Yeah.
是啊。

580
00:25:15.300 --> 00:25:15.960
That's huge.
那太夸张了。

581
00:25:16.400 --> 00:25:16.860
Huge.
太夸张了。

582
00:25:17.140 --> 00:25:25.800
Well, they put it up in our parking lot between the two sound stages, and they put, like, a green padded platform around it.
他们把它竖在两个摄影棚之间的停车场里，还在周围放了一个绿色软垫平台。

583
00:25:25.880 --> 00:25:26.720
In case you fell?
以防你掉下来？

584
00:25:26.960 --> 00:25:27.200
Yep.
没错。

585
00:25:27.200 --> 00:25:33.460
And they put up a big green screen behind the whole thing, and they put up a big green screen behind the whole thing, and then they brought Rain out along with, like,
他们在整个装置后面竖起了一个巨大的绿幕，然后把雷恩带出来，随行的还有，

586
00:25:33.520 --> 00:25:37.280
a stunt coordinator and a safety officer, and they had Rain climb up.
一位特技协调员和一名安全员，他们让雷恩爬了上去。

587
00:25:37.320 --> 00:25:39.780
It was only a few feet that he had to climb.
他其实只需要爬几英尺高。

588
00:25:50.020 --> 00:25:52.400
They superimpose, like, one pole onto the other.
他们把两根杆子的画面叠加在了一起。

589
00:25:52.500 --> 00:25:52.840
Yes.
是的。

590
00:25:52.840 --> 00:25:53.380
Got it.
明白了。

591
00:25:53.660 --> 00:26:01.100
Even though Rain was really only a little bit off the ground, they could, like, hike it up so it looked like he was, like, halfway up the pole.
尽管雷恩离地其实只有一点点高，但他们可以通过后期处理，让他看起来像是爬到了杆子中间。

592
00:26:01.320 --> 00:26:01.560
Yeah.
没错。

593
00:26:01.920 --> 00:26:03.220
That's movie magic, folks.
这就是电影魔法，伙计们。

594
00:26:03.220 --> 00:26:04.780
That is some good movie magic.
那确实是高超的电影魔法。

595
00:26:05.060 --> 00:26:06.980
But here's the thing that gets me about that.
但关于这一点，最让我感慨的是，

596
00:26:07.200 --> 00:26:15.740
That's, like, real special effects kind of, like, stunty stuff for our little TV show about a paper company.
对于我们这个关于造纸公司的小型电视剧来说，这简直是真正的特效特技了。

597
00:26:15.740 --> 00:26:24.200
Like, I never really thought hard about how much work it took to do that gag until we went to break it down.
我以前从没认真想过为了那个恶作剧花了多少心血，直到我们开始拆解分析它。

598
00:26:24.380 --> 00:26:24.720
Yeah.
是啊。

599
00:26:24.900 --> 00:26:25.020
Right?
对吧？

600
00:26:25.420 --> 00:26:30.100
Like, it's such a quick little blip, and you're like, that was, like, two weeks of figuring that out.
那只是转瞬即逝的一个小片段，你会觉得，天哪，为了搞定那个镜头竟然花了两个星期。

601
00:26:30.160 --> 00:26:30.740
Of prep.
关于介词。

602
00:26:30.920 --> 00:26:31.240
Yeah.
是啊。

603
00:26:31.480 --> 00:26:39.440
I feel like every week we are learning how much Michael Gallenberg, Kyle Alexander, Phil Shea, our wardrobe department, set designers,
我觉得每周我们都在了解迈克尔·加伦伯格、凯尔·亚历山大、菲尔·谢伊，还有我们的服装部门、布景设计师们，

604
00:26:39.520 --> 00:26:43.280
how they all made these little moments happen and made it seamless.
他们是如何让这些小细节成真，并让一切显得天衣无缝的。

605
00:26:43.580 --> 00:26:43.780
Yeah.
没错。

606
00:26:44.360 --> 00:26:45.040
I know.
我知道。

607
00:26:45.040 --> 00:26:46.920
So much work goes into these little things.
这些小细节背后投入了大量的工作。

608
00:26:47.040 --> 00:26:47.840
It's amazing.
太惊人了。

609
00:26:48.000 --> 00:26:49.240
The fruit fly wrangler.
果蝇饲养员。

610
00:26:49.380 --> 00:26:51.720
We had to know their, like, mating cycle.
我们还得了解它们的，比如，交配周期。

611
00:26:52.240 --> 00:26:52.720
Craziness.
太疯狂了。

612
00:26:52.920 --> 00:26:53.160
It's crazy.
真是疯狂。

613
00:26:53.620 --> 00:26:55.020
Well, that was the cold open.
好吧，那是片头小剧场。

614
00:26:55.440 --> 00:26:57.880
Now we start this episode.
现在我们开始这一集。

615
00:26:58.140 --> 00:26:58.960
Michael's in his office.
迈克尔在他的办公室里。

616
00:26:58.960 --> 00:27:00.340
He's on the phone with David Wallace.
他正在和戴维·华莱士通电话。

617
00:27:00.680 --> 00:27:05.560
I feel like David's really playing Michael here because he dangles out that regional supervisor job.
我觉得戴维在这里真的在耍迈克尔，因为他抛出了那个区域主管职位的诱饵。

618
00:27:05.680 --> 00:27:07.720
He's like, you know, I still haven't filled that slot yet.
他说，你知道，我还没填补那个空缺呢。

619
00:27:08.120 --> 00:27:09.360
And Michael's like, oh.
迈克尔就说，哦。

620
00:27:09.780 --> 00:27:12.200
And then he asked Michael to go do this thing.
然后他让迈克尔去做这件事。

621
00:27:12.360 --> 00:27:12.780
Yeah.
是啊。

622
00:27:12.780 --> 00:27:15.640
To go spy on this tiny little paper company.
去监视那家小小的造纸公司。

623
00:27:15.860 --> 00:27:16.560
I know.
我知道。

624
00:27:16.740 --> 00:27:18.460
To do some field work.
去做些实地考察。

625
00:27:18.780 --> 00:27:20.220
Michael's so excited.
迈克尔太兴奋了。

626
00:27:20.660 --> 00:27:21.740
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

627
00:27:22.280 --> 00:27:28.100
During this scene, I was really struck by the toys on Michael's desk because they would rotate them.
在这一幕中，迈克尔桌上的玩具真的吸引了我，因为他们会轮换这些玩具。

628
00:27:28.320 --> 00:27:28.940
They would, you guys.
他们真的会换，伙计们。

629
00:27:28.940 --> 00:27:30.700
Every once in a while, there would be some new toys.
每隔一段时间，就会出现一些新玩具。

630
00:27:30.940 --> 00:27:32.200
Here's what was on his desk.
这是他桌上的东西。

631
00:27:32.420 --> 00:27:33.660
A Rubik's Cube.
一个魔方。

632
00:27:33.980 --> 00:27:34.800
Not finished.
没拼好。

633
00:27:35.120 --> 00:27:35.420
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

634
00:27:35.620 --> 00:27:37.280
A tiny pool table.
一个微型台球桌。

635
00:27:37.680 --> 00:27:38.160
Yes.
没错。

636
00:27:38.520 --> 00:27:41.580
A colorful plastic expanding ball thingy.
一个彩色的塑料伸缩球玩意儿。

637
00:27:41.980 --> 00:27:43.120
You know that thingy?
你知道那个玩意儿吗？

638
00:27:43.180 --> 00:27:43.520
Yeah, yeah.
知道，知道。

639
00:27:43.660 --> 00:27:44.440
That's a staple.
那是标配。

640
00:27:44.680 --> 00:27:44.920
Yes.
是的。

641
00:27:45.040 --> 00:27:46.160
And also the wind-up teeth.
还有那个发条牙齿玩具。

642
00:27:46.300 --> 00:27:47.140
Those are always there.
那些总是摆在那儿。

643
00:27:47.140 --> 00:27:49.600
But the pool table had moved.
但台球桌换了位置。

644
00:27:49.620 --> 00:27:51.440
So he's clearly played it recently.
所以他显然最近玩过它。

645
00:27:51.480 --> 00:27:54.160
And it's on top of all the stuff in his inbox.
而且它就压在他收件箱里所有的东西上面。

646
00:27:54.340 --> 00:27:56.320
He can't get to anything in his inbox.
他根本没法处理收件箱里的任何东西。

647
00:27:56.580 --> 00:27:57.440
It's not important.
那不重要。

648
00:27:57.700 --> 00:28:00.500
The pool table is number one of things to do.
台球桌才是头等大事。

649
00:28:00.720 --> 00:28:00.900
Yeah.
是啊。

650
00:28:01.340 --> 00:28:02.080
It made me laugh.
这让我笑了。

651
00:28:03.780 --> 00:28:08.960
A miniature pool table in his inbox says everything you need to know about Michael Scott's work ethic.
他收件箱里那个微型台球桌，足以说明迈克尔·斯科特的工作态度了。

652
00:28:09.280 --> 00:28:09.720
That's right.
没错。

653
00:28:10.240 --> 00:28:15.480
Stanley and Phyllis are going to start having this conversation about whether or not they think Hillary Swank is hot.
斯坦利和菲利斯开始讨论他们觉得希拉里·斯万克到底漂不漂亮。

654
00:28:15.960 --> 00:28:17.840
And the rest of the gang gets involved.
然后其他人也都参与了进来。

655
00:28:18.060 --> 00:28:21.600
I feel like these kind of moments happen in small offices.
我觉得这种时刻在小办公室里很常见。

656
00:28:21.840 --> 00:28:23.540
You sort of start to debate things.
你们会开始争论一些事情。

657
00:28:23.680 --> 00:28:29.140
Like you pick a soccer team during the playoffs and people debate about the players and it can become a whole thing.
就像季后赛时你选了一支足球队，大家就会争论球员表现，最后闹得不可开交。

658
00:28:29.260 --> 00:28:31.000
And it's just a way to fill the boredom.
这只是打发无聊的一种方式。

659
00:28:31.120 --> 00:28:31.740
Oh, for sure.
噢，确实。

660
00:28:32.080 --> 00:28:33.820
I have a bone to pick with Jim.
我对吉姆有点意见。

661
00:28:34.120 --> 00:28:34.840
Why is that?
为什么？

662
00:28:35.060 --> 00:28:38.900
At 3 minutes 18 seconds, I titled this moment, What the Hell, Jim?
在3分18秒的时候，我把这一刻命名为：搞什么鬼，吉姆？

663
00:28:39.100 --> 00:28:40.080
What is the moment?
那一刻发生了什么？

664
00:28:40.500 --> 00:28:43.200
Jim suggests they put it to a vote in the bullpen.
吉姆提议在办公区进行投票。

665
00:28:43.940 --> 00:28:45.960
Angela says she isn't voting.
安吉拉说她不参与投票。

666
00:28:46.300 --> 00:28:48.020
And Jim says nobody cares.
然后吉姆说没人会在意。

667
00:28:48.760 --> 00:28:49.000
Oh.
噢。

668
00:28:49.560 --> 00:28:50.600
What the hell, Jim?
搞什么鬼，吉姆？

669
00:28:50.800 --> 00:28:51.920
That's some Jim sass.
那是吉姆式的刻薄。

670
00:28:52.040 --> 00:28:52.260
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

671
00:28:52.420 --> 00:28:53.140
Jim sass.
吉姆式的刻薄。

672
00:28:53.380 --> 00:28:55.160
Did you notice what Pam said?
你注意到帕姆说了什么吗？

673
00:28:55.360 --> 00:28:56.300
What did Pam say?
帕姆说了什么？

674
00:28:56.600 --> 00:28:59.420
Pam says, Did you see her with her bangs?
帕姆说：你看到她留刘海的样子了吗？

675
00:28:59.760 --> 00:29:00.240
Oh!
噢！

676
00:29:01.160 --> 00:29:06.840
And lady, this made me laugh out loud because I have just recently gotten bangs.
天哪，这让我大笑出声，因为我最近刚剪了刘海。

677
00:29:07.100 --> 00:29:09.220
And people have a lot of opinions about it.
大家对这事儿意见可多了。

678
00:29:09.400 --> 00:29:11.240
They do have opinions about my bangs.
他们确实对我的刘海很有意见。

679
00:29:11.400 --> 00:29:18.100
But what made me laugh was that before I got my bangs, I, of course, Googled images of people with bangs.
但让我发笑的是，在我剪刘海之前，我当然在谷歌上搜过留刘海的人的照片。

680
00:29:18.100 --> 00:29:19.320
You have to do research.
你得做做功课。

681
00:29:19.780 --> 00:29:19.920
Yeah.
是啊。

682
00:29:19.920 --> 00:29:22.480
You don't just, you got to look at all the pictures.
你不能随随便便就剪，你得看看所有的照片。

683
00:29:22.760 --> 00:29:24.100
You Googled people with bangs.
你谷歌了留刘海的人。

684
00:29:24.280 --> 00:29:26.700
You texted me, I think I'm going to get bangs.
你给我发短信说，我想我要去剪刘海了。

685
00:29:26.900 --> 00:29:27.040
Yeah.
是啊。

686
00:29:27.420 --> 00:29:29.020
To which I replied, oh, no.
我回复说，噢，千万别。

687
00:29:29.440 --> 00:29:35.380
I said, I think I'm going to get bangs right now because, like, I was getting a haircut in the moment.
我说，我想我现在就要去剪刘海了，因为当时我正好在理发店。

688
00:29:35.800 --> 00:29:37.180
By the time you replied, it was done.
等你回复的时候，我已经剪完了。

689
00:29:37.360 --> 00:29:37.840
I know.
我知道。

690
00:29:38.040 --> 00:29:40.800
I was like, oh, I was busy with the kids.
我当时在忙着照顾孩子。

691
00:29:40.880 --> 00:29:42.020
I decided we were going to paint.
我决定带他们画画。

692
00:29:42.140 --> 00:29:44.140
I bought the canvas and all the paint stuff were outside.
我买了画布，把颜料什么的都搬到了外面。

693
00:29:44.160 --> 00:29:45.460
We'd made this huge mess.
我们弄得一团糟。

694
00:29:45.580 --> 00:29:47.780
I'd set my phone aside so I didn't get paint on it.
我把手机放在一边，免得沾上颜料。

695
00:29:47.880 --> 00:29:50.300
And then I just thought I'd check in, see what's happening.
后来我心想看看手机，了解一下情况。

696
00:29:50.300 --> 00:29:56.080
And I see this text from you that's half an hour old that says, I think I'm going to get bangs now.
结果看到你半小时前发来的短信，说：我想我现在要去剪刘海了。

697
00:29:56.180 --> 00:29:56.820
And I was like, oh, no.
我当时就想，噢，不。

698
00:29:56.980 --> 00:29:58.260
I didn't get to weigh in.
我都没来得及发表意见。

699
00:29:58.420 --> 00:29:59.900
But, lady, I think they're adorable.
但是，亲爱的，我觉得你的刘海很可爱。

700
00:30:00.060 --> 00:30:01.800
I think they're super cute because they're curly.
我觉得它们超级可爱，因为是卷的。

701
00:30:02.100 --> 00:30:02.920
I'm loving it.
我超喜欢这个。

702
00:30:03.160 --> 00:30:07.660
I bring it up because one of the people I saw in my research was Hilary Swank with bangs.
我提起这个是因为我在做调研时看到的人里有留着刘海的希拉里·斯万克。

703
00:30:07.760 --> 00:30:10.440
So when Pam said this in the scene, it made me laugh.
所以当帕姆在戏里说这句话时，我笑了。

704
00:30:10.860 --> 00:30:16.980
But I really based my bangs on some, like, Mia Farrow from Hannah and Her Sisters.
但我的刘海造型其实参考了《汉娜姐妹》里的米娅·法罗。

705
00:30:16.980 --> 00:30:21.800
You look very 70s, kind of, like, beachy wave with bangs.
你看上去很有70年代的感觉，有点像那种海滩波浪卷配刘海。

706
00:30:22.120 --> 00:30:23.820
A little bit of Terry Garr.
还有点泰瑞·加尔的味道。

707
00:30:24.480 --> 00:30:27.340
Terry Garr wore some bangs like no one's business.
泰瑞·加尔留起刘海来那可是无人能及。

708
00:30:27.440 --> 00:30:27.780
That's right.
没错。

709
00:30:27.940 --> 00:30:31.420
But my main inspiration was probably Stevie Nicks.
但我主要的灵感来源大概是史蒂薇·尼克斯。

710
00:30:31.940 --> 00:30:37.960
And I will admit that after getting my bangs, I did style my hair in a full Stevie Nicks.
我得承认，剪了刘海后，我确实给自己做了个全套的史蒂薇·尼克斯造型。

711
00:30:38.020 --> 00:30:40.680
And then I took pictures and I put them side by side.
然后我拍了照片，把它们放在一起对比。

712
00:30:40.800 --> 00:30:41.840
I was too shy to poSt.
我太害羞了，没敢发出来。

713
00:30:42.080 --> 00:30:43.900
I want to see the side by side.
我想看对比照。

714
00:30:43.900 --> 00:30:45.100
You want to see my Stevie Nicks picture?
你想看我的史蒂薇·尼克斯造型照？

715
00:30:45.100 --> 00:30:46.440
Do you have it on your phone?
你手机里有吗？

716
00:30:46.440 --> 00:30:46.760
Yeah.
有。

717
00:30:46.920 --> 00:30:47.860
I mean, I really did this.
我是说，我真的这么做了。

718
00:30:48.200 --> 00:30:49.080
Oh, my God.
天哪。

719
00:30:49.260 --> 00:30:50.580
This is amazing.
这太棒了。

720
00:30:52.480 --> 00:30:54.400
Oh, you kind of did the same mouth expression.
噢，你连嘴部的表情都模仿得一模一样。

721
00:30:54.400 --> 00:30:55.020
I tried it.
我试过了。

722
00:30:55.100 --> 00:30:56.260
I put on the same necklace.
我还戴了同款项链。

723
00:30:56.300 --> 00:30:57.740
I did, like, a whole thing.
我真的全套都做了。

724
00:30:57.800 --> 00:30:58.620
Oh, you did.
噢，你真的做了。

725
00:30:58.920 --> 00:31:01.460
We got to put that in Office Ladies Pod Stories, please.
我们一定要把它放进《办公室女士》的播客故事里，拜托了。

726
00:31:01.900 --> 00:31:02.260
Okay.
好的。

727
00:31:02.260 --> 00:31:05.940
I mean, I'm doing a whole pouty mouth, so I got a little bit, like, shy.
我是说，我当时在做那种嘟嘴的表情，所以觉得有点害羞。

728
00:31:06.200 --> 00:31:07.780
You even did the dark eyeliner.
你连深色眼线都画了。

729
00:31:07.880 --> 00:31:08.180
I did.
是的。

730
00:31:08.340 --> 00:31:09.240
I'm telling you.
我跟你说。

731
00:31:09.320 --> 00:31:10.320
She was my inspo.
她就是我的灵感来源。

732
00:31:10.320 --> 00:31:11.480
This was a whole afternoon.
这可是花了我整个下午。

733
00:31:12.020 --> 00:31:13.620
I thought I knew your life.
我以为我很了解你的生活。

734
00:31:13.620 --> 00:31:14.660
This was a whole day.
这可是花了我一整天。

735
00:31:14.660 --> 00:31:15.860
I didn't know what was happening.
我当时都不知道发生了什么。

736
00:31:15.860 --> 00:31:18.600
I mean, I had to take off my glasses for the picture.
我是说，为了拍照我不得不摘掉眼镜。

737
00:31:18.740 --> 00:31:19.120
I know.
我知道。

738
00:31:19.460 --> 00:31:21.820
Which actually made it a little hard to take the picture.
这其实让拍照变得有点困难。

739
00:31:22.080 --> 00:31:22.180
Honey.
亲爱的。

740
00:31:22.180 --> 00:31:23.200
Because I couldn't see very well.
因为我看得不太清楚。

741
00:31:23.260 --> 00:31:23.980
Tell me about it.
谁说不是呢。

742
00:31:24.040 --> 00:31:26.680
I can't tell you how many photos I've taken of Josh and the kids.
我数不清给乔什和孩子们拍过多少照片了。

743
00:31:26.760 --> 00:31:29.960
Because, you know, when you're like a family, one parent has to take the picture.
因为你知道，当一家人在一起时，总得有一个家长负责拍照。

744
00:31:30.100 --> 00:31:30.200
Yeah.
是啊。

745
00:31:30.480 --> 00:31:33.460
And half the time I don't have my glasses because I'm not good about wearing them.
而且有一半时间我都没戴眼镜，因为我不习惯戴。

746
00:31:33.680 --> 00:31:36.680
And Josh will be like, babe, these are out of focus.
乔什就会说，宝贝，这些照片都失焦了。

747
00:31:36.680 --> 00:31:38.000
I'm like, I can't tell.
我就说，我看不出来。

748
00:31:38.580 --> 00:31:39.440
I just click.
我只管按快门。

749
00:31:39.440 --> 00:31:42.820
I love how we literally could not be more off topic right now.
我喜欢我们现在完全跑题了这一点。

750
00:31:42.840 --> 00:31:43.460
We are so off topic.
我们跑题跑得太远了。

751
00:31:43.620 --> 00:31:43.760
Okay.
好的。

752
00:31:43.900 --> 00:31:44.120
All right.
行吧。

753
00:31:44.180 --> 00:31:45.040
We'll get back to it.
我们回头再说这个。

754
00:31:45.040 --> 00:31:45.780
Let's get back on topic.
我们回到正题吧。

755
00:31:45.940 --> 00:31:46.200
All right.
好吧。

756
00:31:46.280 --> 00:31:46.500
All right.
行。

757
00:31:46.560 --> 00:31:46.740
All right.
好的。

758
00:31:46.780 --> 00:31:48.440
So we are now.
所以我们现在是这样。

759
00:31:48.660 --> 00:31:49.280
Oh, God.
天哪。

760
00:31:49.420 --> 00:31:52.000
You guys, we are about to talk about a scene I absolutely loved.
伙计们，我们接下来要聊一个我超级喜欢的场景。

761
00:31:52.060 --> 00:31:54.260
It's a driving scene between Dwight and Michael.
那是德怀特和迈克尔的一场开车戏。

762
00:31:54.500 --> 00:31:56.180
They're headed to Prince Family Paper.
他们正前往普林斯家族造纸公司。

763
00:31:56.900 --> 00:32:00.360
Did you notice how much they bicker in this scene?
你们注意到他们在这场戏里吵得有多厉害了吗？

764
00:32:00.360 --> 00:32:01.700
They're like an old married couple.
他们就像一对老夫老妻。

765
00:32:01.900 --> 00:32:02.620
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

766
00:32:02.620 --> 00:32:05.760
They bicker about who would seduce the fictional daughter.
他们争论谁会去诱惑那个虚构出来的女儿。

767
00:32:06.060 --> 00:32:07.720
They don't even know if this person exists.
他们甚至都不知道这人是否存在。

768
00:32:08.340 --> 00:32:10.380
And they bicker about Denny's and IHOP.
他们还为了丹尼餐厅和国际煎饼屋吵架。

769
00:32:10.500 --> 00:32:12.020
They bicker about the clouds.
他们连云都要吵。

770
00:32:12.580 --> 00:32:13.920
Dwight says, get your clouds right.
德怀特说，把你的云搞搞清楚。

771
00:32:14.020 --> 00:32:15.280
Michael tells them to shut up.
迈克尔叫他们闭嘴。

772
00:32:16.580 --> 00:32:18.800
But I have a background catch.
但我发现了一个背景细节。

773
00:32:19.040 --> 00:32:19.700
What is it?
是什么？

774
00:32:19.860 --> 00:32:22.860
Oh, it sent me down a Google path, Jenna.
噢，这让我去谷歌上查了个底朝天，珍娜。

775
00:32:23.460 --> 00:32:23.840
All right.
好吧。

776
00:32:24.020 --> 00:32:27.720
So whenever we have driving scenes, we always look for palm trees, right?
每当有开车戏时，我们总是会找棕榈树，对吧？

777
00:32:27.920 --> 00:32:28.080
Yeah.
没错。

778
00:32:28.240 --> 00:32:29.200
Spot the palm tree.
找找棕榈树。

779
00:32:29.520 --> 00:32:32.160
In this one, I recognize the street they were on.
在这一场里，我认出了他们所在的街道。

780
00:32:32.620 --> 00:32:33.580
It's Chandler Boulevard.
那是钱德勒大道。

781
00:32:33.800 --> 00:32:35.180
It's a residential street.
那是一条住宅区街道。

782
00:32:35.340 --> 00:32:36.660
And guess what else I recognized?
你们猜我还认出了什么？

783
00:32:36.900 --> 00:32:37.120
What?
什么？

784
00:32:37.360 --> 00:32:38.360
It was trash day.
那天是垃圾回收日。

785
00:32:38.980 --> 00:32:42.220
And there were blue recycle bins in every driveway.
每家每户的车道上都有蓝色的回收桶。

786
00:32:42.220 --> 00:32:43.540
I took a few photos.
我拍了几张照片。

787
00:32:43.760 --> 00:32:44.040
Okay.
好的。

788
00:32:44.380 --> 00:32:45.820
I'll put those in pod.
我会把它们放到播客里。

789
00:32:46.280 --> 00:32:49.700
So then I thought, is that what the recycle trash bins look like in Scranton?
于是我就想，斯克兰顿的回收垃圾桶长那样吗？

790
00:32:50.360 --> 00:32:55.100
So that took me to the recycling laws for Lackawanna County.
于是我就去查了拉克瓦纳县的回收法规。

791
00:32:55.340 --> 00:32:55.620
Oh.
噢。

792
00:32:56.000 --> 00:32:59.700
Hang with me because there's a woman named Barbara who I am now fascinated by.
听我说完，因为有个叫芭芭拉的女人，我现在对她着迷了。

793
00:33:00.340 --> 00:33:04.400
First of all, that is not what recycle bins look like in Lackawanna County.
首先，拉克瓦纳县的回收桶根本不是长那样的。

794
00:33:04.580 --> 00:33:07.120
So theirs are like these blue round tubs.
他们那边的是那种蓝色的圆桶。

795
00:33:07.340 --> 00:33:07.580
Okay.
好吧。

796
00:33:07.980 --> 00:33:10.180
Unless they've changed, you guys can correct me.
除非他们换了，你们可以纠正我。

797
00:33:10.520 --> 00:33:12.880
Ours are these like skinny rectangles with lids.
我们这边的是那种带盖子的细长矩形桶。

798
00:33:13.060 --> 00:33:13.200
Yep.
没错。

799
00:33:13.200 --> 00:33:16.080
So here's an article I read from April of 2019.
这是我读到的一篇2019年4月的文章。

800
00:33:17.380 --> 00:33:21.100
Barbara Giovannoli is the recycling coordinator for Lackawanna County.
芭芭拉·乔瓦诺利是拉克瓦纳县的回收协调员。

801
00:33:21.300 --> 00:33:29.220
Barbara shared that the recycling center in Lackawanna County accepts plastics and glass bottles and jars, aluminum, steel cans, as well as newspaper.
芭芭拉分享说，拉卡瓦纳县的回收中心接收塑料、玻璃瓶罐、铝罐、钢罐以及报纸。

