1378
00:55:51.120 --> 00:55:57.100
And then Oscar projects this picture of Hillary Swank's face with all this grid on it, right?
然后奥斯卡投影了一张希拉里·斯万克的脸部照片，上面布满了网格，对吧？

1379
00:55:57.320 --> 00:55:57.580
Yeah.
是啊。

1380
00:55:57.920 --> 00:55:59.740
And he talks about coinophilia.
他谈到了对称偏好。

1381
00:55:59.980 --> 00:56:01.600
The symmetry, right?
就是对称性，对吧？

1382
00:56:01.800 --> 00:56:02.420
Of the face.
脸部的对称性。

1383
00:56:02.420 --> 00:56:15.580
So coinophilia is this, stay with me here, evolutionary hypothesis for explaining why certain animals seek mates that look a certain way.
所以对称偏好是——听我说——一种进化假说，用来解释为什么某些动物会寻找特定长相的配偶。

1384
00:56:15.780 --> 00:56:23.120
And it proposes that animals, including humans, find the symmetry of features most attractive.
它提出包括人类在内的动物，都认为对称的五官最吸引人。

1385
00:56:23.420 --> 00:56:25.040
I read all about it.
我读过相关内容。

1386
00:56:25.160 --> 00:56:26.460
I barely understood it.
我几乎没看懂。

1387
00:56:26.620 --> 00:56:26.880
Okay.
好吧。

1388
00:56:26.880 --> 00:56:28.160
It was very wordy.
那文章太啰嗦了。

1389
00:56:29.000 --> 00:56:37.400
But in ancient Greece, they created something called the golden ratio of beauty, or phi.
但在古希腊，他们创造了一种叫做黄金比例的美学，或者叫“斐”。

1390
00:56:37.760 --> 00:56:39.460
It's a mathematical equation.
这是一个数学方程式。

1391
00:56:39.900 --> 00:56:49.560
And it says if your face possesses a specific set of ratios of distance between the different features on your face,
它说如果你的脸部五官之间的距离符合一套特定的比例，

1392
00:56:49.560 --> 00:56:56.380
they believed it could be mathematically proven that you had a perfect face.
他们认为这在数学上就能证明你拥有一张完美的脸。

1393
00:56:56.840 --> 00:57:03.740
This equation is what da Vinci used when he was creating his Vertruvian man.
这个方程式就是达芬奇在创作《维特鲁威人》时所使用的。

1394
00:57:04.140 --> 00:57:04.580
Oh.
哦。

1395
00:57:05.040 --> 00:57:07.920
That is what Oscar's, I think, really talking about.
我想奥斯卡真正想说的就是这个。

1396
00:57:08.100 --> 00:57:09.800
